  "notes": "KANYE WEST  (The College Dropout era, c. 2001-2004: \"chipmunk soul\")\n\nTECHNIQUE (sourced)\n- GLC: \"we was recording on a Roland VS 1680 in his bedroom\"; samples from a crate of Al Green,\n  Nina Simone and Aretha records (Complex, \"The Making of The College Dropout\").\n- Just Blaze says Kanye used his ASR-10 on the Blueprint and Black Album sessions (Complex).\n- Speeding samples up inside the ASR-10, the MPC2000 and tempos: unconfirmed.\n\nTHIS TEMPLATE\nSoul Chops Sampler (SP Pitch effect on): pitch the pads up for the sped-up vocal character.\nHard rack drums at 58% through a compressor and the built-in Overdrive (The drum rack plays one-shots synthesized for these templates (CC0, no recordings), in the voice of the machine each channel is named for, with a starter beat in the pattern; replace them with your own samples for the real machine.); bass,\nstrings, rap and hook vocals.\n\nMIX NOTES\n- The chop is the lead: carve 2-4 kHz on the strings and keys around it.\n- Drum Bus: built-in bus compression, CHOWTapeModel \"Old MPC\". Master: built-in glue, FL\n  Limiter; -10 to -9 LUFS.\n- Loudness: streaming plays back near -14 LUFS integrated (Spotify), so a louder master is turned down; keep true peak below -1 dBTP.\n\nCOVERAGE\nGood for the chipmunk chop. No ASR-10 model; the drums are synthesized one-shots, not samples of the machines.\n\nSOURCES\nComplex \"The Making of Kanye West's The College Dropout\"; Complex (Just Blaze ASR-10 photo);\nSpotify for Artists, \"Loudness normalization\" (support.spotify.com/us/artists/article/loudness-normalization).\n\nFREE PLUG-INS (download them before opening the template; a missing one keeps its slot)\n- OB-Xf (GPL-3.0): https://github.com/surge-synthesizer/OB-Xf\n- CHOWTapeModel (GPL-3.0): https://chowdsp.com/products.html\n\nSETUP (written from this template)\nTempo 92 BPM, 4/4, key Abmaj, cycle bars 1-4.\n\nTracks\n- Soul Chops (pitched up) (Instrument, +0 dB) -> Music Bus\n    instrument: Sampler (SP-303 model): effect Pitch on, CTRL 1-3 = 60%, 0%, 100%; quantize 16; pad grade standard\n- Drums (Instrument, +0 dB) -> Drum Bus\n    instrument: Channel Rack (synthesized one-shots of the template samples: Kick (909) = kick-909.wav, Snare (LinnDrum) = snare-acoustic.wav, Clap (909) = clap.wav, Hat (909) = hat-909.wav, Open Hat (808) = openhat-808.wav)\n    strip FX: Compressor (Threshold -14, Ratio 4, Attack 15, Release 100, Make-up 2)\n    strip FX: Overdrive (Drive 9, Tone 7000, Level -4, Mix 0.6)\n    region: Step Sequencer pattern with a starter beat (15 steps on), swing 58% (MPC terms), 5 rows = the rack's channels\n- Bass (Instrument, -6 dB) -> Music Bus\n    instrument: Surge Synth Team: OB-Xf: OB-Xf patch \"Basses/Electric Bass 1\"\n- Strings (Instrument, -14 dB) -> Music Bus\n    instrument: Surge Synth Team: OB-Xf: OB-Xf patch \"Strings/String Section Large\"\n    send: Reverb (bus 4) at -12 dB\n- Rap Vocal (Audio, +0 dB) -> Vocal Bus\n    strip FX: Compressor (Threshold -20, Ratio 4, Attack 0.5, Release 60, Make-up 3)\n    strip FX: Compressor (Threshold -22, Release 300, Make-up 3)\n    send: Reverb (bus 4) at -22 dB\n    send: Delay (bus 5) at -24 dB\n- Hook Vocal (Audio, -4 dB) -> Vocal Bus\n    strip FX: Compressor (Threshold -22, Release 300, Make-up 3)\n    send: Reverb (bus 4) at -14 dB\n    send: Delay (bus 5) at -20 dB\n\nBuses (the n-th Aux strip listens to bus n)\n- Drum Bus (bus 1): chowdsp: CHOWTapeModel: factory preset \"Old MPC\"; Compressor (Threshold -16, Ratio 4, Release 100, Make-up 2)\n- Music Bus (bus 2): Compressor (Threshold -16, Ratio 2, Attack 20, Release 300, Make-up 2)\n- Vocal Bus (bus 3): Compressor (Release 150, Make-up 2)\n- Reverb (bus 4): Space D (Dry -96, Wet 0, Decay 1.6, Decay Curve 1, IR \"01.2s Medium Hall\")\n- Delay (bus 5): Tape Delay (Time 652.2, Feedback 0.3, Tone 2000, Mix 1)\n\nStereo Out\n- built-in effects: Compressor (Threshold -12, Ratio 2, Attack 30, Release 200)\n- plug-ins (after the built-in effects): Lemon Limiter: gain +3.5 dB, ceiling -1 dB, other settings default\n\nBring your own samples: no recordings are included.\n",
